# Maven POM & Artifact Standards

## Project Naming Pattern
- Project names follow: `{domain/system}-[subdomain-]-{layer}-api` — **no regional prefix** (deprecated per leadership directive)
- Layer suffixes: `sys` (system), `proc` (process), `exp` (experience)
- Separated by hyphens — no underscores or periods
- Examples: `usps-sys-api`, `aspn-sys-api`, `sfl-exp-api`, `sfl-crm-sys-api`
- Max 42 characters (Anypoint Runtime Manager limit); use short forms if needed: `##-##-sapi`, `##-##-papi`, `##-##-xapi`

## Artifact ID
- The Maven project `<name>` should match the project name.

## Versioning
- Follow semantic versioning: `major.minor.patch` (e.g., `1.0.17`)
- Development versions use `--SNAPSHOT` suffix
- Major bump: breaking changes (renamed resources, structural model changes)
- Minor bump: non-breaking functional additions (new endpoints, enhanced error handling)
- Patch bump: bug fixes, refactoring, documentation

## RAML Dependency
- API spec must be pulled from Anypoint Exchange as a dependency with `raml` classifier and `zip` type
- Keep the RAML spec version in sync with the APIKit configuration

## Maven settings.xml

- **No hardcoded Exchange credentials in POM** — use `settings.xml` for Anypoint Exchange and Mule EE authentication.
- When `settings.xml` is missing or incomplete, ensure it includes the required servers and repositories. See `agents/review/rules/review-maven-settings.mdc`.

## Review Checklist

- [ ] Project name follows `{name}-{layer}-api` pattern (no regional prefix)
- [ ] Version follows semantic versioning
- [ ] No hardcoded Exchange credentials in POM (use settings.xml)
- [ ] settings.xml has required servers (anypoint-exchange-v3, eu-anypoint-exchange-v3, mulesoft-release-ee) and repositories — see review-maven-settings.mdc
- [ ] RAML spec dependency version matches APIKit config
